  "actor": "HARNESS",
  "what": "problem PD-1@v2 drafted",
  "phase": "DEFINE",
  "minute": 124.0,
  "event_seq": 287,
  "root_problem": "Billing dispute tickets roughly doubled from ~600/month (Jun-Jul) to ~1180-1260/month (Aug-Sep 2026, E-07), coincident with validation rule BV-17 deployed 2026-08-01 (E-13). BV-17's high-consumption check compares raw AMI register readings directly to 12-month m3 consumption history with no unit scaling (E-13); AMI firmware v4.2, rolled out 2026-06, reports register readings in 0.1 m3 units versus older firmware's whole m3 units (E-14), so BV-17 misreads normal v4.2 consumption as a ~10x spike. This causes billing import validation to reject valid, on-time AMI reads as \"high consumption\" and substitute an estimate instead: 1184 of the 1240 AMI-channel disputed ESTIMATED-read accounts show exactly this REJECTED_HIGH_CONSUMPTION pattern tagged firmware v4.2 (E-12). The resulting wrong estimated bills drive at least this AMI-metered portion of the surge; response-handling speed is within SLA (E-01) and no tariff change occurred (E-04), ruling out those alternatives. The mechanism behind the larger ACTUAL-read-type dispute share (1785/3025, E-03) is not yet confirmed and is flagged as an open unknown."
 },
